"grader_02_item_03","tb_0336","Tutor A","feedback","physics","tb_0336_c03","diagnosis","critical","The response must identify that the student made an arithmetic error in part c) by equating $\frac{1}{5}$ to $\frac{5}{35}$, when it should be $\frac{7}{35}$. If done correctly, the answer should have been $\frac{1}{7}MR^2\omega_0^2$, not $\frac{3}{35}MR^2\omega_0^2$.","F",""
"grader_02_item_03","tb_0336","Tutor A","feedback","physics","tb_0336_c04","diagnosis","not_critical","The response can explicitly note that the error of using the wrong moment of inertia leads to an incorrect result for both parts a) and b), since the result carry forward.","F",""
